  "reasoning": "The patient reports a cluster of systemic symptoms: feeling hot and sweaty (indicative of fever and perspiration), chills, vomiting, nausea, headache, body aches, and notably, itchy skin. This specific combination—especially the presence of fever/chills paired with severe itching, gastrointestinal distress (vomiting/nausea), headache, and muscle pain—is a classic clinical presentation for malaria. While other febrile illnesses like dengue or typhoid share some overlapping features, the prominent pruritus (itching) alongside these systemic signs strongly aligns with malaria.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]malaria[/DIAGNOSIS]"
